cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  This is a work in progress; results are preliminary and not peer reviewed.
  If you refer to it, please cite it as below and mention the version and the
  access date. All rights reserved (see LICENSE).
title: "Brazilian Port Digital Transformation Observatory: Port Digitalization, Information Quality and Operational Times"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gregory"
    given-names: "Valber"
    email: "valber.gregory@gmail.com"
abstract: >
  Research compendium and information system integrating Brazilian port
  operations (ANTAQ), foreign trade (Comex Stat) and a curated registry of the
  Porto Sem Papel single window dated from official ordinances, used to
  estimate how port digitalization changed vessel times, the information the
  regulator records, technical efficiency and trade costs. Work in progress.
keywords:
  - port digitalization
  - maritime single window
  - information quality
  - digital government
  - difference-in-differences
  - Brazil
repository-code: "https://github.com/valbergregory/Port-Digitalization-Observatory"
url: "https://github.com/valbergregory/Port-Digitalization-Observatory"
license-url: "https://github.com/valbergregory/Port-Digitalization-Observatory/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
